<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Japan=E2=80=99s 10-year benchmark governme=
nt bond hit 3% for the first time in a generation, and is now up almost 5 b=
asis points at 2.99%. The US 10-year Treasury yield rose 2.6bps to 4.78%, t=
he highest since early 2025.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">UK government borrowing costs have risen t=
o the highest since 2008, as higher oil prices stoke inflation fears.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The yield on the 10-year gilt has jumped 7=
 basis points to 5.223%, the highest since June 2008.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Germany=E2=80=99s 10-year yield, the bench=
mark for the eurozone, rose 2 basis points to 3.34%, a fresh 15-year high.<=
/p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Inflation fears have boosted expectations =
of interest rate increases. Markets are pricing in a rate increase in New Z=
ealand on Wednesday, while the European Central Bank is widely expected to =
raise its key interest rates by 0.25 percentage points at its next meeting =
on 10 September. Traders also see a better than even chance of rate rises i=
n the US and Japan this month.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Bank of England is not expected to mov=
e until later this year, with markets pricing in a quarter-point rate incre=
ase to 4% in about November or December.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In Asia, shares were mixed =E2=80=93 Japan=
=E2=80=99s Nikkei was flat, while Hong Kong=E2=80=99s Hang Seng lost 0.8% a=
nd South Korea=E2=80=99s Kospi eked out a 0.2% gain after earlier losses.</=
